        solution: 'W = PΔV = nRΔT = 2.0 × 8.314 × 100 = 1663 J. ΔU = (3/2)nRΔT = 2494 J. Q = ΔU + W = (5/2)nRΔT = 4157 J. Constant-pressure heating needs more heat than constant-volume heating because some energy leaves as work.',
        calc: ['2.0 * P.C.R * 100', '1.5 * 2.0 * P.C.R * 100', '2.5 * 2.0 * P.C.R * 100'], answers: [1663, 2494, 4157],
